{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q420958","formula":"Al₂(SO₄)₃(H₂O)₁₂·5H₂O","hill":"Al2H34O29S3","elements":["H","O","Al","S"],"composition":{"H":34.0,"O":29.0,"S":3.0,"Al":2.0},"names":{"en":"Alunogen","ru":"Алуноген","uk":"Алуноген"},"descriptions":{"en":"Alunogen (from French alun, \"alum\"), also called feather alum and hair salt is a colourless to white (although often coloured by impurities, such as iron substituting for aluminium) fibrous to needle-like aluminium sulfate mineral. It has the chemical formula Al2(SO4)3·17H2O. It is often found on the walls of mines and quarries as a secondary mineral. It can be found in the oxidation zones of some ore deposits as well as on burning coal dumps (i.e., as the product of millosevichite hydration).","ru":"Алуноген — минерал, водный сульфат алюминия. Название означает «производный от квасцов». Другое название — алюноген.","uk":"Алуноґен, алюноґен (рос. алуноген; англ. alunogen; нім."},"fame":18,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":null,"structure":null,"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q420958","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alunogen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%90%D0%BB%D1%83%D0%BD%D0%BE%D0%B3%D0%B5%D0%BD","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (uk)","url":"https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%90%D0%BB%D1%83%D0%BD%D0%BE%D0%B3%D0%B5%D0%BD","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"photo","name":"Wikimedia Commons","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alunogen_-_Almyras,_Agia_Varvara,_Cyprus.jpg","license":"CC BY 3.0"}],"similar":[{"id":"Q26840944","formula":"AlH₂₄KO₂₀S₂","names":{"en":"Potassium alumi